# Wiki dock orientation: {{WIKI_NAME}}

This repo is docked to the **{{WIKI_NAME}}** wiki (companion
`{{COMPANION}}`): the wiki is this repo's durable memory - session
handoffs land there as append-only events, curated workstreams hold the
living state of each goal, and the garden pipeline keeps both clean.
This repo's `.wiki/` dock is only the pointer; the wiki holds the
content.

- Wiki root on this machine: `{{WIKI_ROOT}}`
- Dock identity: `.wiki/manifest.toml`; machine-local overlay:
  `.wiki/local.toml` (never committed, per the dock posture)
- Every kit CLI resolves the wiki through the dock: run commands from
  anywhere in this repo, no `--wiki` flag needed.

## Project skills rendered into this repo

{{SKILL_DIRS}}

## Commands a session needs

```sh
# record a session handoff (the handoff skill drives this)
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-event.py new-handoff --help
# apply a handoff to its workstream (the garden skill drives this)
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-garden.py --help
# re-render the wiki's projections (log, orientation index)
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-render.py log
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki-render.py claude-local
# working-tree integrity check
uv run --project {{KIT_ROOT}} {{KIT_ROOT}}/scripts/wiki_doctor.py
```

Generated by `wiki-dock install`; reinstall to refresh. Edit the wiki's
config, not this file.
